From: vLLM FusenCache team
Subject: [PATCH] fix(models/gemma4_mm): avoid aliasing scheduler's is_mm_embed
 double-buffer in embed_input_ids

Gemma4ForConditionalGeneration.embed_input_ids() crashes with a CUDA
illegal memory access once the v1 engine runs >=4 concurrent requests with
async scheduling and cudagraph_mode=FULL:

    File ".../vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4_mm.py", line 1257, in embed_input_ids
        is_multimodal = is_multimodal.to(input_ids.device)
    torch.AcceleratorError: CUDA error: an illegal memory access was
    encountered

`is_multimodal` is a slice view into gpu_model_runner.is_mm_embed_buffers[i].gpu.
The buffer pair is double-buffered on the CPU side only; the GPU storage
of each buffer is re-used every other iteration. With async scheduling,
iteration N+2's non-blocking copy_to_gpu() can overwrite the same GPU
bytes while iteration N's in-flight CUDA-graph replay is still reading
them from torch.where(is_multimodal, zeros_like(input_ids), input_ids).
The `.to()` line is simply the next CUDA API call and therefore where the
deferred error surfaces.

Two surgical changes:

1. Only take the PLE-mask path when real multimodal embeddings are
   present. Gemma3n's equivalent method feeds input_ids straight into
   get_per_layer_input_embeddings(); Gemma4 added the mask kernel and with
   it the racy read. Text-only batches (the common case for conversational
   serving) now bypass the mask entirely, matching Gemma3n semantics.

2. When the mask is genuinely needed, clone `is_multimodal` onto our own
   storage (and force the device cast to blocking) so downstream kernels
   do not alias the scheduler's shared double-buffer. The clone is a
   bool[n] tensor - sub-microsecond on modern GPUs.

Fixes concurrent-batch crashes reproducible with:
  - Gemma4 (e.g., 26B NVFP4)
  - cudagraph_mode=FULL, prefix caching on, chunked prefill on
  - --async-scheduling (the default)
  - Any attention backend slower than FlashAttention (FusenCache k4v4b64,
    custom quantized KV caches, etc.) - the wider forward window makes the
    race easy to hit.

Related prior art: the companion async-scheduling fix in
gpu_model_runner.synchronize_input_prep() (CUDA event + stream barrier)
addresses the same failure *class* but a *different* code path; it fences
input_ids / block_tables between steps, not the is_mm_embed buffers that
are read inside `_preprocess`.

Backport note: vLLM 0.19.1 and earlier do not ship gemma4_mm.py (Gemma4
support was added on main after 0.19.1). No backport required.

---
 vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4_mm.py | 31 ++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 1 file changed, 25 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4_mm.py b/vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4_mm.py
--- a/vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4_mm.py
+++ b/vllm/model_executor/models/gemma4_mm.py
@@ -1219,13 +1219,32 @@ class Gemma4ForConditionalGeneration(nn.Module, SupportsMultiModal, SupportsPP):
         if self.per_layer_embeddings is not None:
             # Mask multimodal tokens (image/audio) to 0 for PLE
             # computation (using token_type_ids == 0 as text_mask).
             # Replicate this: map image token positions to token 0.
-            if is_multimodal is not None:
-                is_multimodal = is_multimodal.to(input_ids.device)
-                ple_input_ids = torch.where(
-                    is_multimodal, torch.zeros_like(input_ids), input_ids
-                )
-            else:
+            #
+            # `is_multimodal` is a slice view into the gpu_model_runner's
+            # shared `is_mm_embed_buffers` double-buffer. The CPU side is
+            # double-buffered to hide the prep-vs-forward race, but the
+            # GPU storage of each buffer is reused every other iteration.
+            # Running `torch.where(is_multimodal, ...)` on that view while
+            # iteration N+2's non_blocking=True copy_to_gpu() is in flight
+            # produces a CUDA illegal memory access under async scheduling
+            # + cudagraph_mode=FULL. Mitigate both ways:
+            #   (a) skip the mask kernel entirely when no multimodal
+            #       embeddings are actually present (matches Gemma3n), and
+            #   (b) when the mask is needed, clone onto our own storage so
+            #       downstream kernels no longer alias the scheduler buffer.
+            has_mm_embeds = multimodal_embeddings is not None and (
+                isinstance(multimodal_embeddings, torch.Tensor)
+                or len(multimodal_embeddings) > 0
+            )
+            if is_multimodal is not None and has_mm_embeds:
+                is_multimodal = is_multimodal.to(
+                    input_ids.device, non_blocking=False
+                ).clone()
+                ple_input_ids = torch.where(
+                    is_multimodal, torch.zeros_like(input_ids), input_ids
+                )
+            else:
                 ple_input_ids = input_ids

             per_layer_inputs = self.language_model.model.get_per_layer_inputs(
